<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  REV Trustee - Phase 3 security role, shipped as a solution component (WBS 6.1, automation
  #6, Trustee Review Portal).

  Held by trustees - named individual tenant users (Kevin and colleagues on the Revitalise
  board), never a service account. Reaches Application/Review/Grant data only through the
  trustee Code App (ADR-003) - "no direct table access" in TAD section 6.1 describes the
  experience, not the role: the Code App's managed Dataverse connector still runs as the
  signed-in trustee, so this role is exactly what gates what that connector can return.
  TAD section 6.2's own row for this persona: "Read on Application, Review, Grant - filtered
  by REV_TrusteeRestricted. Write verdict + notes on Review. Read Anonymised Statistic. No
  direct table access; reaches data through the app only. No export-to-Excel privilege - the
  offline route is the anonymised pack (FR-032/FR-039)."

  rev_review (WBS 6.4) landed in this solution DURING this same session, concurrently with
  this file - see Entities/rev_review/Entity.xml's own header, which explicitly flags "the
  REV Trustee role must grant Update on rev_verdict1/rev_verdict2/rev_notes1/rev_notes2
  only" for "whoever builds WBS 6.1". That table-level privilege is granted below. THE
  COLUMN-SCOPING PART OF THAT INSTRUCTION CANNOT BE EXPRESSED BY A SECURITY ROLE - flagged,
  not silently done, immediately below the rev_review privileges. rev_anonymisedstatistic
  (WBS 8.1, a different automation) did NOT land and is still deferred.

  HOW THIS ROLE IS ASSIGNED
  Never directly to a user in TST/ACC or PRD. The only approved mechanism is
  Entra security group -> Dataverse group team (type AAD Security Group) -> this role,
  applied by provisioning/dataverse/bind-roles-to-groups.ps1 which looks the role up BY NAME
  because role GUIDs differ per environment (C-TECH-040, TAD section 6.1, ADR-008). Direct
  assignment is permitted in DEV only. Per the group-team mapping table (TAD section 6.1) the
  group team is "REV Trustees", backed by Entra security group
  REV-PP-GrantApplications-Trustees-<env>.

  THIS IS A NEW CUSTOM ROLE, NOT A MODIFIED OUT-OF-BOX ROLE (C-TECH-046).
  TAD section 6.2 records the deliberate decision NOT to use a shared "[PREFIX] Base User"
  base-plus-additive role, because this role must have no access to Provider or Setting - a
  shared base would either over-grant or be empty. Each persona role is therefore
  self-sufficient, which is why the platform baseline block below is the same block that
  "REV Admin" and "REV Service Automation" carry.

  WARNING FOR THE REVIEWER - narrower than for the first two roles, but not closed.
  The platform baseline block's PRIVILEGE NAMES are already confirmed to exist in this
  Dataverse environment: they are the exact post-correction set validated live on 2026-08-14
  when REV Admin and REV Service Automation were created (prvReadSavedQuery and
  prvReadEnvironmentVariableValue removed, both confirmed absent from this environment; see
  those two files' own headers). Copying that confirmed set here is therefore lower risk than
  the original guess was. What is still UNVERIFIED for this role specifically: (1) the role
  has never itself been created in DEV, so the create-role event (step 5 of
  ensure-schema.ps1) is unproven for a third role even though the privilege names it will
  request are known good; (2) whether the full MDA-shaped baseline (personal views,
  web resources) is the right set for a persona that only ever opens a Code App, never the
  model-driven app, is a genuine open question with no ground truth yet - no Code App
  exists (WBS 6.2/6.3 build it). Candidate Unvalidated Assumptions Register row (renumber at
  merge into the feature Dev Summary section 10 - Dev Summary currently ends at A-002):

    A-TR-1 | Claim: the MDA-oriented platform baseline block (prvReadUserQuery/Create/
    Write/Delete "Basic", prvReadWebResource "Global") is necessary and sufficient for a
    Code-App-only persona, not merely harmless | Where: RolePrivileges block below, the
    "Platform baseline" section | Evidence: E3 - by analogy with the two sibling roles,
    which are MDA personas; no Code App exists to test the narrower alternative against |
    Why not verified: no live Code App yet (WBS 6.2, 6.3) | Cheapest verification: after the
    Code App is built and shared (WBS 6.5), sign in as a test trustee, use the app end to
    end, then remove one baseline privilege at a time in a DEV-only copy of the role and
    confirm nothing breaks, OR leave as is if TST/ACC/PRD parity with the other two roles is
    preferred over minimality | Status: OPEN

  COLUMN-LEVEL SECURITY IS NOT IN THIS FILE, AND FOR THIS ROLE IT IS THE WHOLE CONTROL.
  Table privileges below make rows visible; they do not release a single secured column.
  This role is DELIBERATELY ABSENT from REV_TrusteeRestricted's membership - see
  Other/FieldSecurityProfiles.xml's own header and
  provisioning/dataverse/ensure-column-security-profile-members.ps1, whose membership list
  is "REV Admins and REV Service Accounts, and nothing else". That is not an oversight this
  role file works around; it is the mechanism TAD section 6 and ADR-002 rely on: every one
  of the 51 secured columns on rev_applicant/rev_application - including
  rev_narrativeraw - stays unreadable to any principal holding this role, in every
  environment, regardless of the table-level Read privilege below. Do not add this role, or
  the "REV Trustees" group team, to that profile's membership. Confirmed present as "REV
  Admins" and "REV Service Accounts" only, and unchanged by this feature, on 2026-08-21.

  AMENDED 2026-08-21 (WBS 6.1) - prvReadrev_applicant ADDED, RESOLVING A TAD CONTRADICTION.
  TAD section 3.1 (the rev_applicant attribute table) marks rev_agerange and
  rev_locationarea "trustee-visible (FR-027)", both IsSecured=0 on
  Entities/rev_applicant/Entity.xml. TAD section 6.2's own row for this persona gives
  "Read on Application, Review, Grant" - Applicant is absent - and this role, as
  originally built, carried no privilege on rev_applicant at all. Column security
  releases a COLUMN; it never grants table Read. Without table Read on rev_applicant a
  trustee cannot read the ROW, so a column marked trustee-visible on that table was
  unreachable regardless of REV_TrusteeRestricted - and rev_locationarea is where
  FR-034's "region" comes from (there is no region column on rev_application;
  rev_breaklocation is the break's location, a different thing, confirmed by reading
  every attribute on both entities), so the list screen could not have met
  FR-034/US-012 AC-1/US-013 AC-1 as this role stood. This is a DERIVED amendment to the
  TAD in the direction section 3.1 and FR-027/FR-034 require, not a correction of a
  mistake in THIS file - flagged as a proposed TAD amendment for the reviewer, in the
  same style as the rev_nonqualificationreason amendment (TAD section 3.1,
  2026-08-16). ALTERNATIVE REJECTED: denormalising rev_agerange/rev_locationarea onto
  rev_application at intake, so the trustee's existing Application-only read would
  reach them without a new table privilege. Rejected because it would change
  Automation #1 (the scoring flow already reads these off rev_applicant), duplicate
  personal-adjacent derived data onto a second table, and widen rather than narrow the
  footprint of tables carrying applicant-derived data - the opposite of what ADR-002's
  separation exists for.

  RESOLUTION IS TABLE READ ONLY - COLUMN SECURITY IS COMPLETELY UNCHANGED.
  prvReadrev_applicant added at Global, read-only (no Create/Write/Delete/Append/
  AppendTo), in the Feature table privileges block below. This role remains, and MUST
  REMAIN, absent from REV_TrusteeRestricted's membership (see the WARNING paragraph
  above and Other/FieldSecurityProfiles.xml's own header - both read in full and both
  unchanged by this amendment). rev_applicant carries twelve IsSecured=1 columns -
  rev_title, rev_firstname, rev_lastname, rev_fullname, rev_email, rev_phone,
  rev_addressline, rev_addressline2, rev_towncity, rev_postcode, rev_dateofbirth,
  rev_gender - confirmed by reading every attribute in
  Entities/rev_applicant/Entity.xml and cross-checked one-for-one against
  Other/FieldSecurityProfiles.xml's rev_applicant FieldPermission entries, which list
  exactly these twelve and no others. With table Read granted and profile membership
  unchanged, every one of those twelve still masks to nothing for this role; only the
  seven IsSecured=0 columns become newly readable - rev_name (the pseudonymised
  autonumber reference, ADR-013, never the applicant's actual name), rev_agerange,
  rev_locationarea, rev_applicanttype, rev_preferredcontactmethod,
  rev_lastcontactdate, rev_privacynoticeacceptedon.

  LIVE-VERIFIED 2026-08-21 against DEV (read-only; no write attempted, per IMP-0084/
  IMP-0133): `privileges?$filter=name eq 'prvReadrev_applicant'` returns exactly one
  row (privilegeid 4e7bc1d2-f14e-43de-9cc9-5ce6dcff85a4) - the privilege name this
  role's ensure-schema.ps1 step-5 resolution depends on already exists in this
  environment because rev_applicant itself already exists there, so step 5 needs no
  change and will not report FAILED for this addition. Also re-confirmed in the same
  pass: `roles?$filter=name eq 'REV Trustee'` still returns zero rows (A-TR-2
  unaffected), and REV_TrusteeRestricted's `teamprofiles_association` in DEV is
  currently an empty array - no team is a member yet in this environment, "REV
  Trustees" included, which is consistent with (not evidence against) the intended
  TST/ACC and PRD membership of exactly REV Admins and REV Service Accounts.

  Candidate register row (renumber at merge into the feature Dev Summary section 10 -
  A-TR-1 through A-TR-4 already proposed above and in
  provisioning/dataverse/share-apps.ps1):

    A-TR-5 | Claim: granting prvReadrev_applicant (Global, read-only) makes rows on
    rev_applicant readable to this role while REV_TrusteeRestricted's non-membership
    continues to mask all twelve IsSecured=1 columns on that table, so the net change
    is exactly the seven trustee-visible/operational columns named above and nothing
    more | Where: this RolePrivilege, cross-checked against
    Entities/rev_applicant/Entity.xml (every attribute's IsSecured flag) and
    Other/FieldSecurityProfiles.xml (the profile's rev_applicant FieldPermission list)
    | Evidence: E1 for the column-set claim (read directly from both source files);
    E1 for the privilege-name claim (live DEV query, above) | Why flagged anyway: a
    security-relevant table-Read addition should carry its reasoning for the reviewer
    to check, not just a bare privilege line | Not yet verified: the actual masking
    behaviour against a live trustee identity - that needs a real trustee test user and
    the Code App (WBS 6.2/6.3/6.5), which do not exist yet; this is a source-and-
    metadata check, not an end-to-end proof | Status: OPEN pending that end-to-end
    check; the source-level and metadata-level facts above are settled, not guesses.

  THE id ABOVE IS A SENTINEL, NOT A FABRICATED GUID (C-TECH-051, C-TECH-052).
  Unlike REV Admin and REV Service Automation - which already exist in DEV and whose id
  attributes were fixed 2026-08-14 by reading the real roleid back live - "REV Trustee" does
  not exist anywhere yet (confirmed live against DEV, 2026-08-21: `roles?$filter=name eq
  'REV Trustee'` returns zero rows). Roles are one of the platform types matched strictly by
  id on import (see the sibling roles' own headers): declaring a fabricated-but-plausible
  GUID here would either coincidentally collide with nothing today and then fail outright
  the first time this solution is imported into an environment that already has a
  same-named, different-id role, or - the more likely and more dangerous case - pack and
  import cleanly today and simply be wrong, with nothing to detect it until the next import
  disagrees. A real GUID is also indistinguishable from a real GUID by any gate, so a
  fabricated one is invisible to review. The sentinel below is chosen to be impossible for
  any environment to ever assign (Dataverse-issued GUIDs are lower-case hex in 8-4-4-4-12
  groups; this string contains letters outside a-f and is the wrong shape), so it fails
  loudly instead of silently:

    A-TR-2 | CLOSED 2026-08-21. `pwsh provisioning/dataverse/ensure-schema.ps1 -Env dev`
    reported CREATED for "REV Trustee" and every privilege below (exit 0). Real id read
    back live via `roles?$filter=name eq 'REV Trustee'&$select=roleid,name`:
    `3ab6cc7b-959d-f111-b8de-70a8a5079a1b`, at the root business unit. Substituted below,
    exactly as 2026-08-14's fix did for the other two roles (REV Admin.xml line ~40) -
    unlike Entities/OptionSets/FieldSecurityProfiles, roles are matched strictly by id on
    import, so a fabricated id would have packed and imported cleanly while being wrong.
    The matching `<RootComponent type="20" id="{3ab6cc7b-959d-f111-b8de-70a8a5079a1b}"/>`
    is added to Other/Solution.xml in the same change - both sides agree, per
    `scripts/verify-solution-root-components.py`. This id is correct for DEV only: TST/ACC
    and PRD get their own Dataverse-assigned ids when Pipelines promotes the role there for
    the first time (see REV Admin.xml's note on the same property).
-->
<Role id="{3ab6cc7b-959d-f111-b8de-70a8a5079a1b}" name="REV Trustee">
  <IsInherited>2</IsInherited>
  <BusinessUnit>
    <IsRoot>1</IsRoot>
  </BusinessUnit>
  <IsCustomizable>1</IsCustomizable>
  <CanBeDeleted>1</CanBeDeleted>
  <IntroducedVersion>1.0.0.0</IntroducedVersion>
  <RolePrivileges>
      <!-- ===== Feature table privileges ===== -->
      <!-- List/detail screens (WBS 6.2, 6.3): score, region, dates, status, holiday
           details. No prvWrite/Create/Delete/Append - a trustee never edits a case
           through this role; the only write this persona makes is the verdict, which
           lands on rev_review (see DEFERRED below), never on rev_application itself. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadrev_application" level="Global" />
      <!-- Grant-level detail (holiday dates, acceptance status) shown on the detail
           screen. Same no-write reasoning as rev_application. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadrev_grant" level="Global" />
      <!-- rev_review (WBS 6.4, landed this session): read the panel round - both
           trustees' verdicts, notes, the staff recommendation and outcome, so a
           trustee reviewing the record can see what has already been decided. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadrev_review" level="Global" />
      <!-- ADDED 2026-08-21 (WBS 6.1) - RESOLVES A TAD CONTRADICTION, SEE THE FILE
           HEADER FOR THE FULL REASONING (search "AMENDED 2026-08-21"). TAD section 3.1
           marks rev_applicant.rev_agerange and rev_applicant.rev_locationarea
           "trustee-visible (FR-027)" - rev_locationarea is where FR-034's "region" comes
           from, and FR-034 is this role's own acceptance criterion (US-012 AC-1, US-013
           AC-1) - but TAD section 6.2's row for this persona lists Read on "Application,
           Review, Grant" only, Applicant absent, and this role as built carried no
           privilege on rev_applicant at all. Column security releases a COLUMN; it never
           grants table Read - so without this privilege the trustee-visible columns TAD
           section 3.1 promises were unreachable, because the ROW itself could not be read.
           READ-ONLY, GLOBAL, DELIBERATELY: no Create/Write/Delete/Append/AppendTo - a
           trustee never edits applicant data, same reasoning as rev_application/rev_grant
           above. THIS DOES NOT REVERSE THE "NO IDENTITY ACCESS" DECISION BELOW: this role
           remains, and MUST REMAIN, absent from REV_TrusteeRestricted's membership (see
           the WARNING earlier in this header and Other/FieldSecurityProfiles.xml's own
           header) - table Read makes the ROW visible; REV_TrusteeRestricted's column
           security still masks all twelve IsSecured=1 columns on rev_applicant
           (rev_title, rev_firstname, rev_lastname, rev_fullname, rev_email, rev_phone,
           rev_addressline, rev_addressline2, rev_towncity, rev_postcode, rev_dateofbirth,
           rev_gender) for every principal that is not a profile member, this role
           included. Only the seven IsSecured=0 columns become newly readable: rev_name
           (the pseudonymised autonumber reference, ADR-013 - never the applicant's actual
           name), rev_agerange, rev_locationarea, rev_applicanttype,
           rev_preferredcontactmethod, rev_lastcontactdate, rev_privacynoticeacceptedon.
           See A-TR-5 in the header. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadrev_applicant" level="Global" />
      <!-- Write the verdict and notes (WBS 6.4 decision capture; FR-037). PLATFORM
           LIMITATION, FLAGGED RATHER THAN SILENTLY ASSUMED SOLVED:
           Entities/rev_review/Entity.xml's header asks for the trustee role to grant
           "Update on rev_verdict1/rev_verdict2/rev_notes1/rev_notes2 only" - but a
           Dataverse security-role privilege is TABLE-LEVEL, not column-level. The
           ONLY platform mechanism that restricts write to specific columns is a field
           security profile on a column with IsSecured=1, and rev_review's own header
           deliberately sets IsSecured=0 on every column (Tier 3, no identifier, and
           the special-category register decision recorded there). So prvWriterev_review
           below grants Update on the WHOLE row - rev_paneldate, rev_round,
           rev_trustee1/2, rev_staffrecommendation, rev_outcome,
           rev_nonqualificationreason and rev_finalisedon included - not only the four
           columns the entity file names. In practice the Code App's own UI is what
           will confine a trustee to editing rev_verdict1/2 and rev_notes1/2 (client-
           side, not a security control): a trustee who called the Dataverse Web API
           directly, bypassing the app, could write any column this privilege covers,
           including rev_finalisedon - the very guard the Finalise Decisions flow (WBS
           6.6) relies on to stop double-execution. Candidate register row (renumber at
           merge): A-TR-4 | Claim: table-level Write is an acceptable substitute for the
           column-scoped restriction Entities/rev_review/Entity.xml asks for | Where:
           this privilege | Evidence: none - this is a known platform gap, not a guess
           | Why not verified: no alternative exists at the role-privilege level |
           Cheapest mitigation: if rev_finalisedon (or another non-verdict column)
           needs a real server-side guard against a direct API write by a trustee, it
           needs IsSecured=1 + a field security profile excluding REV Trustee - a
           change to Entities/rev_review/Entity.xml and FieldSecurityProfiles.xml, both
           out of this file's scope and both owned by other agents this session |
           Status: OPEN, flagged to the reviewer rather than fixed unilaterally. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvWriterev_review" level="Global" />
      <!-- No prvCreaterev_review / prvDeleterev_review / prvAppendrev_review /
           prvAppendTorev_review. TAD section 3.1 says only "trustees write verdict and
           notes only"; nothing in source says a trustee creates the round's review
           row. OPEN QUESTION, not settled here: something must create one rev_review
           row per application per round before a trustee can write to it, and the
           source does not yet say what. If WBS 6.4's decision-capture screen turns
           out to create that row itself (rather than a service-identity process
           pre-creating it), this role will additionally need prvCreaterev_review -
           flag for whoever builds 6.4. -->
      <!-- ===== Platform baseline - see WARNING above ===== -->
      <!-- Read own personal settings - required to open any model-driven app, and by
           extension any client (including a Code App's Dataverse connector) that
           authenticates as this user. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadUserSettings" level="Local" />
      <!-- Update own personal settings (time zone, language, default pane). -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvWriteUserSettings" level="Local" />
      <!-- Create the personal settings row on first sign-in. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvCreateUserSettings" level="Local" />
      <!-- Resolve user lookups (e.g. an application's owner) rendered on screen. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadUser" level="Local" />
      <!-- Resolve the owning business unit shown on every record. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadBusinessUnit" level="Local" />
      <!-- Read organisation-level settings such as date format and base currency. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadOrganization" level="Global" />
      <!-- Resolve the group team the role arrives through (C-TECH-040). -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadTeam" level="Local" />
      <!-- Resolve own role membership; required by the platform's own access checks. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadRole" level="Local" />
      <!-- Required by any money-typed column rendered on the detail screen (holiday
           cost fields, if surfaced) - without it those columns render blank, matching
           the reasoning in the two sibling roles. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadTransactionCurrency" level="Global" />
      <!-- Read own personal views. See A-TR-1 above - kept for parity with the sibling
           roles pending a Code App to test the narrower alternative against. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadUserQuery" level="Basic" />
      <!-- Create own personal views. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvCreateUserQuery" level="Basic" />
      <!-- Update own personal views. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvWriteUserQuery" level="Basic" />
      <!-- Delete own personal views. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvDeleteUserQuery" level="Basic" />
      <!-- Read the icons and resources a model-driven app loads. See A-TR-1 above. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadWebResource" level="Global" />
      <!-- Read the three environment variable definitions this solution ships. Kept for
           parity with the sibling roles; this role's own screens are not currently
           known to read one directly. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadEnvironmentVariableDefinition" level="Global" />
      <!-- prvReadrev_anonymisedstatistic - TAD section 6.2 gives this role "Read
           Anonymised Statistic". CLOSED (WBS 0.4 remainder): this comment used to defer
           the privilege because rev_anonymisedstatistic did not exist in this solution
           yet (EX-001) - it now does (Entities/rev_anonymisedstatistic/), so the
           privilege is added below rather than left deferred. Read-only, Global: nothing
           in TAD section 6.2's row for this persona grants a trustee any write on this
           table, and there is no design reason for one - the table is a staff/service-
           written outcome snapshot (FR-055), not something a trustee records. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadrev_anonymisedstatistic" level="Global" />
      <!-- ===== DELIBERATELY ABSENT - these omissions are controls, not gaps ===== -->
      <!-- No prvExportToExcel of any kind (TAD section 6.6, C-DOM-021): "The REV Trustee
           role carries no export-to-Excel privilege - the sanctioned offline route is
           the anonymised pack (FR-032/FR-039)." This is the one privilege the TAD names
           by exact platform identifier rather than by table, so it is called out here
           even though - like every other privilege not listed in this file - it is
           already absent by simple omission. -->
      <!-- No prvCreaterev_application / prvWriterev_application / prvDeleterev_application
           / prvAppendrev_application / prvAppendTorev_application. A trustee never edits
           case data; the only write this persona ever makes is the verdict + notes on
           rev_review, never on the application record itself (TAD section 6.2; least
           privilege, C-DOM-020). -->
      <!-- No prvWriterev_grant / prvCreaterev_grant / prvDeleterev_grant / append
           privileges - same reasoning; a trustee reads grant context, never edits it. -->
      <!-- No prvCreaterev_review / prvDeleterev_review / prvAppendrev_review /
           prvAppendTorev_review - see the comment beside prvWriterev_review above for
           the reasoning and the open question about what DOES create the row. -->
      <!-- prvReadrev_applicant IS granted above (see "Feature table privileges" -
           ADDED 2026-08-21). This comment used to say the opposite ("No rev_applicant
           privilege of any kind") when TAD section 6.2's row for this persona did not
           list Applicant; that was superseded when TAD section 3.1's trustee-visible
           columns on rev_applicant (rev_agerange, rev_locationarea, FR-027/FR-034) were
           found to need table Read to be reachable at all. THE CONTROL THAT REMAINS IS
           COLUMN SECURITY, NOT TABLE-LEVEL ABSENCE: this role is still, and must stay,
           absent from REV_TrusteeRestricted's membership (see the header WARNING and
           Other/FieldSecurityProfiles.xml), which is what keeps every identity column on
           this table dark regardless of the table Read granted above. Do not restore this
           comment's original wording as a reason to remove the privilege - that would put
           the TAD contradiction this file resolved back in place and fail FR-034. -->
      <!-- No rev_setting privilege of any kind. Thresholds and configuration are an
           admin concern (TAD section 6.6); a trustee has no business reason to read or
           change them. -->
      <!-- No rev_provider privilege of any kind. TAD section 6.2's row for this persona
           does not include Provider, and no Phase 3 portal screen surfaces it. -->
      <!-- No rev_bankaccount or rev_payment privilege of any kind. STALE UNTIL WBS 0.4's
           remainder: this comment used to say these tables did not exist yet. Both now
           exist (Entities/rev_bankaccount/, Entities/rev_payment/) - corrected rather than
           deleted, per this project's own convention. The reason was never "not built yet";
           it was always NFR-002 / separation of duties - bank details sit behind the Finance
           role and one role only, and this role holds no privilege on either table now that
           both are built, exactly as this comment always said would remain true. -->
      <!-- No rev_errorlog privilege of any kind. Operational failures are an admin/
           service concern; a trustee has no reason to see them. -->
      <!-- No prvReadWorkflow. This role never manages or views flow run history - that
           is Admin/Service Automation territory, not a trustee concern. -->
      <!-- No prvAssign / prvShare on any table. This identity never hands a record to
           anyone. -->
      <!-- No audit-deletion privilege (prvDeleteAuditPartition or equivalent), and no
           Dataverse System Administrator / Power Platform Administrator - same
           separation as the other two roles (TAD section 6.5, C-DOM-012). -->
  </RolePrivileges>
</Role>
